{
  "_about": "Motion maps for the film's moving stills. scripts/film-motion.py turns each stop here into public/film/motion/<name>.png. Coordinates are shares of the image named in 'image' (the frame the stop rests on). A region's flow is a direction scaled by speed (0 to 1), or radial from 'center'. 'shimmer' (0 to 1) drives the ripple and the twinkle. 'key' keeps only pixels whose luminance is between lo and hi and whose saturation is under sat (and over minsat); it limits shimmer and flow alike. 'exclude' polygons hold their area still. What moves: water ripples (Doha, the Alberta lake, the Counties river), traffic sliding along a road, thin clouds and haze drifting as one sheet (the stop sets jitter 0 and no billow; a billowing warp wobbled on steam, fog and big clouds, which play loops instead). A 'conveyor' stop (the production line and its model) writes a different map: see Conveyor in components/film/movingStill.ts and build_conveyor in the script.",
